window.docContents[165].resolve({"/Induction/#Logical-Foundations--Induction___-Proof-by-Induction--Review":{"contents":"To prove the following theorem, which tactics will we need besides\nintro and rfl?  (A) none, (B) rewrite, (C) cases, (D) both\nrewrite and cases, or (E) can't be done with the tactics we've seen.    theorem review1 : (true || false) = true\n/- review1 -/\ntheorem review1 : (true || false) = true := by rfl\n\n\nWhat about the next one?    theorem review2 : ∀ b, (true || b) = true\nWhich tactics do we need besides intro and rfl?  (A)\nnone (B) rewrite, (C) cases, (D) both rewrite and cases,\nor (E) can't be done with the tactics we've seen./- review2 -/\ntheorem review2 : ∀ b : Bool, (true || b) = true := by\n  intro b\n  rfl\n\n\nWhat if we change the order of the arguments of ||?    theorem review3 : ∀ b, (b || true) = true\nWhich tactics do we need besides intro and rfl?  (A)\nnone (B) rewrite, (C) cases, (D) both rewrite and cases,\nor (E) can't be done with the tactics we've seen./- review3 -/\ntheorem review3 : ∀ b : Bool, (b || true) = true := by\n  intro b\n  cases b with\n  | false => rfl\n  | true  => rfl\n\n\nWhat about this one?  (Recall that in Lean, Nat.add recurses on the second\nargument: n + zero = n by definition, and n + (m + 1) = (n + m) + 1 by\ndefinition.)    theorem review4 : ∀ n : Nat, n + zero = n\n(A) none, (B) rewrite, (C) cases, (D) both rewrite and cases, or (E)\ncan't be done with the tactics we've seen./- review4 -/\ntheorem review4 : ∀ n : Nat, n + zero = n := by\n  intro n\n  rewrite [add_zero]\n  rfl\n\n\nWhat about this?    theorem review5 : ∀ n : Nat, zero + n = n\n(A) none, (B) rewrite, (C) cases, (D) both rewrite and cases,\nor (E) can't be done with the tactics we've seen./- review5 -/\n/-\n  This one CANNOT be proved by rfl, cases, or rewriting alone --\n  it needs induction!  (We'll see why below.)\n-/\n\n\nWe use this theorem later,\n   so let's make it into a review exercise here\n\n\nProve the following theorem, using theorems from Basics:\n\ntheorem succ_eq_add_one : ∀ n : Nat, succ n = n + one := by\n  solution!\n    intro n\n    rewrite [one_eq_succ_zero, add_succ, add_zero]\n    rfl\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Logical Foundations\u0009Induction: Proof by Induction","header":"3.2. Review","id":"/Induction/#Logical-Foundations--Induction___-Proof-by-Induction--Review"}});